--  MT: monster targets
--
--  Wraps the tower monsters so they can be aimed at wherever the script already aims at players.
--  Used by the shared aim provider dc, which backs both the aimbot and silent aim
--  (Aimbot.TargetMonsters).
--
--  The tower modes (Zombie Tower / Gargoyle Tower, DuelLogic "Gargoyle Tower") put you in a
--  NumTeams=1 duel: there are no enemy PLAYERS at all, so every EnemyByPlayer sweep in the script
--  comes up empty. The monsters are not fighters -- they live in EnemyController as ClientEnemy
--  objects (Players.<me>.PlayerScripts.Controllers.EnemyController, field _model_to_enemy) and the
--  only thing the game tags on them is the "Entity" tag on the model plus "EntityHitbox" on the
--  hitbox parts.
